{"kind":"assert","text":"Follow-up defect found while fixing #15777, not repaired in this lane: head news with request or promise lifecycle is unacknowledgeable. Shape: a child request C resting on the review promise P, sequenced after review request R (the exact child-request shape AGENTS.md step 1 mandates for mid-flight work), or a second promise on R. matches() reads C as news (basis == target.Promise), RequiredAcknowledgments demands it, Build appends it to rests_on and the client signs; the resident's SplitVerdictBases then refuses \"more than one request\" (or \"more than one promise\"), and omitting C refuses as unacknowledged news. No acknowledgment set satisfies both halves. The fold refuses independently (fold.go reportClaim: a report citing a request other than the one its promise answers is ineffective; two promises is disputed), so the repair is not to admit the citation but to change how such news is acknowledged, for example recording it in head_news_acknowledged without appending it to rests_on, or excluding lifecycle-kind statements from the acknowledgment set while still showing them. A smaller inconsistency in the same site: SplitVerdictBases keys on statement.Lifecycle regardless of effectiveness, while the fold counts only effective bases, so a retired or ineffective child request is refused by the guard and ignored by the fold. Evidence verified at b0dc8101 on request/review-news-symmetry (reviewguard.go matches/RequiredAcknowledgments/Build/SplitVerdictBases; fold.go reportClaim). Planner: this needs its own request; it is outside the conditions of #15777 and I am not filing it against myself."}